From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:24:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gdhcp: unicast OFFER and ACK as RFC 2131 asks

send_packet_to_client() broadcast every OFFER and ACK to a client that
had no address yet (ciaddr 0), whether or not the client set the
broadcast bit. RFC 2131 4.1 says the server unicasts those to the
client's hardware address and yiaddr unless the broadcast bit is set,
and broadcasts only then.

The difference matters on a hotspot whose stations do not get group
addressed frames from the access point: a FuriPhone FLX1s (MediaTek) on
a Q25's hotspot (MediaTek) receives unicast fine but never a broadcast,
so it never saw an OFFER and fell back to a link-local address, while
other clients worked.

Broadcast when the client asks for it, unicast to ciaddr when it has
one, otherwise unicast to the client's MAC and yiaddr, and broadcast
only as the last resort.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gdhcp/server.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gdhcp/server.c b/gdhcp/server.c
index 52ea2a5..acc5f65 100644
--- a/gdhcp/server.c
+++ b/gdhcp/server.c
@@ -516,15 +516,33 @@ static void send_packet_to_client(GDHCPServer *dhcp_server,
 	const uint8_t *chaddr;
 	uint32_t ciaddr;
 
-	if ((dhcp_pkt->flags & htons(BROADCAST_FLAG))
-				|| dhcp_pkt->ciaddr == 0) {
+	/*
+	 * RFC 2131 4.1: broadcast only when the client asks for it with the
+	 * broadcast bit. A client that already has an address (ciaddr) gets
+	 * it there; one that has none yet gets the OFFER or ACK unicast to
+	 * its hardware address and the offered address (yiaddr).
+	 *
+	 * Broadcasting regardless cost clients that do not receive group
+	 * addressed frames from the access point - a MediaTek station on a
+	 * MediaTek hotspot, for one - their lease, while unicast reached
+	 * them fine.
+	 */
+	if (dhcp_pkt->flags & htons(BROADCAST_FLAG)) {
 		debug(dhcp_server, "Broadcasting packet to client");
 		ciaddr = INADDR_BROADCAST;
 		chaddr = MAC_BCAST_ADDR;
-	} else {
+	} else if (dhcp_pkt->ciaddr) {
 		debug(dhcp_server, "Unicasting packet to client ciaddr");
 		ciaddr = dhcp_pkt->ciaddr;
 		chaddr = dhcp_pkt->chaddr;
+	} else if (dhcp_pkt->yiaddr) {
+		debug(dhcp_server, "Unicasting packet to client yiaddr");
+		ciaddr = dhcp_pkt->yiaddr;
+		chaddr = dhcp_pkt->chaddr;
+	} else {
+		debug(dhcp_server, "Broadcasting packet to client");
+		ciaddr = INADDR_BROADCAST;
+		chaddr = MAC_BCAST_ADDR;
 	}
 
 	dhcp_send_raw_packet(dhcp_pkt,
